 "final_result": "Completed the full CsPbBr3 band-structure workflow from scratch.\n\nMaterials Project ID: mp-600089 (CsPbBr3, Pm-3m #221).\nAtom count: 5 atoms before and after primitive-cell reduction (the base CIF was already the primitive cell: 1 Cs, 1 Pb, 3 Br; a=5.9486 A).\n\nWorkflow outline:\n1. generate_cif fetched the base structure (mp-600089, Pm-3m #221) into structures/base.cif. The cell was already primitive (5 atoms), so no reduction was needed.\n2. generate_structures.py (ran OK, returncode 0): wrote 51 structures (structure_000.cif unperturbed, structure_001-050.cif perturbed with thermal displacements at 300 K + 0.5% random strain). RMS displacements from literature Debye-Waller U values: Br=0.1225 A, Pb=0.0894 A, Cs=0.1095 A. nat/ntyp asserted per structure.\n3. Pseudopotentials fetched (fr, pbesol, nc, stringent, UPF, hint_level=normal): Cs (z_valence=9, 25 Ha), Pb (z_valence=22, 44 Ha), Br (z_valence=17, 38 Ha). All fully relativistic with spin-orbit.\n4. setup_jobs.py (ran OK, returncode 0): created calculations/000-050/ with PP files, kpath.json, pw.in, bands.in, bands_post.in. Settings: ecutwfc=88 Ry (44 Ha x 2), ecutrho=352 Ry, noncolin=.true., lspinorb=.true., occupations='fixed', conv_thr=1e-8, nbnd=100, SCF k-mesh 5x5x5. validate_qe_input passed for both pw.in and bands.in.\n5. run_espresso_workflow on calculations/000: success=true, all 3 steps completed (SCF 18.6s, bands 171.6s, post 37.0s).\n6. plot_bands.py (ran OK, returncode 0): plotted band structure aligned to VBM, saved calculations/000/bands_000.pdf.\n\nASE functions used: ase.io.read (CIF), ase.io.write (CIF), ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in (pw.x inputs), ase.Atoms (structure representation). No pymatgen.\n\nBand gap obtained: 0.391 eV (VBM=4.589 eV, CBM=4.980 eV in raw QE output; aligned to VBM=0 in the plot). This is significantly smaller than the experimental 1.78 eV, which is expected for a DFT calculation with PBEsol (known to underestimate band gaps, especially for halide perovskites where hybrid functionals or GW corrections are needed).\n\nScientific assumptions:\n- T=300 K for thermal displacements: CsPbBr3 cubic phase is stable at room temperature (unlike CsPbI3 which needs >350 K).\n- Literature Debye-Waller U values for displacement amplitudes (no frequency needed, unlike Einstein model).\n- Fixed occupations (semiconductor, gap 1.78 eV from MP).\n- Fully relativistic pseudopotentials with spin-orbit for all elements (Pb Z=82, Cs Z=55 both >54; Br Z=35 <54 but all PPs in the same table are fr for consistency).\n- nbnd=100 (82 electrons with spin-orbit, each band holds 1 electron, so n_occupied=82).\n\nItems needing expert review:\n- The DFT band gap (0.391 eV) is much smaller than the experimental 1.78 eV. This is a known limitation of PBEsol for halide perovskites. A hybrid functional (HSE06) or GW calculation would be needed for a quantitatively accurate gap.\n- The 5x5x5 SCF k-mesh may be slightly under-sampled for a 5.95 A cubic cell; a 6x6x6 or 8x8x8 mesh could be considered for production-quality results.\n- The Debye-Waller U values used for thermal displacements are approximate literature values; a phonon calculation would give more accurate temperature-dependent displacements.",
